== Scalar and usefulness limits
The span checker uses F1000003 for its written row-space test. In both g4/F19 membership modes, split-only rank1 becomes rank9 in both augmented representations. This is not DLP rank at a verified subgroup order: the chosen scalar may not divide the Jacobian order. The remaining ten cells have unchanged rank. No target solving or useful-log-rank gain follows from this generic-scalar observation.

The separate genus2 subgroup-modulus experiment shows zero rank increment in all six cells. Current evidence therefore supports the restricted span construction, not a tenfold complete-cost premise, novelty, fastest-tool or benchmark-promotion claim. The next discriminating test is subgroup-modulus useful rank and completion with all coordinates/partial rows retained, frozen separately before execution.

